 services are available for access. Click on the tab to navigate to the service-specific page.",serviceCards:{downloadAadhaar:{title:"Download Aadhaar",description:"Click here to download digitally signed and password protected electronic copy of the Aadhaar."},orderPVC:{title:"Order Aadhaar PVC Card",description:"Click here to order a secure, wallet-sized Aadhaar PVC card."},updateAadhaarOnline:{updateAadhaarOnline:"Update Aadhaar Online",updateAadhaar:"updateAadhaar",headerTitle:"Please select the type of Online Aadhaar Update",title:"Address Update",description:"Click here to update the Address of your Aadhaar. For any other update, kindly visit nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra"},bankLinkingStatus:{title:"Bank Linking Status",description:"Click here to check the Aadhaar and bank account linking status."},generateVirtualID:{title:"Generate Virtual ID",description:"Virtual ID(VID) can be used in-lieu of the Aadhaar number. Click here to download 16 digits random VID."},offlineEkyc:{title:"Offline eKYC",description:"Click here to access secure and shareable eKYC document, used for offline identification verification."},lockUnlockBiometrics:{title:"Lock / Unlock Biometrics",description:"Click here to temporarily lock/unlock your biometrics information."},lockUnlockAadhaar:{title:"Lock / Unlock Aadhaar",description:"Click here to temporarily lock/unlock your Aadhaar. Please use this service carefully."},paymentHistory:{title:"Payment History",description:"Click here to view the payment and refund status."},hofRequests:{title:"My Head of Family(HoF) Requests",description:"Click here to check HoF based Address Sharing Requests"},aadharUpdateHistory:{title:"Aadhaar Update History",description:"Click here to find your Aadhaar update history."},bankSeedingStatus:{title:"Bank Seeding Status",description:"Click here to find your Bank Seeding Status."},authenticationHistory:{title:"Authentication History",description:"Click here to view the authentication history",heading:"Please select Authentication Date Range to Fetch Authentication History",modality:"Select Modality",fieldStartText:"Enter Start Date",fieldEndText:"Enter End Date",button:"Fetch Authentication History",tableHeading:"Your Selection has resulted in {{txnNumber}} Authentications",dateRange:"Aadhaar number holder can view details of upto 50 authentication records performed by any Authentication User Agency (AUA) or by him/her in the last 6 months.",filterName:"Select Modality",note:{l1:"Note: ",l2:"AUA Transaction Id: ",l3:"Unique Aadhaar transaction Id at the time of request.",l4:"List of Authentication User Agency: ",l5:"In case of any issues regarding a transaction, contact the AUA for that transaction. ",l6:"Click here to view details.",l7:"Authentication Response: ",l8:"Success / Failure",l9:"UIDAI Error Codes: ",l10:"Aadhaar authentication error codes. ",l11:"Click here",l12:"FAQs: ",l13:"Authentication Transaction History. ",l14:"Click here",l15:"Auth Modality: ",l16:"Method of Aadhaar Authentication",l17:"The Authentication History PDF Password will be in 8 characters. Combination of the first four letters of your name (as in Aadhaar) in CAPITAL letters and Year of Birth in YYYY format."}},documentUpdate:{title:"Document Update",description:"Click Here to upload your Proof of Identity (PoI) and Proof of Address (PoA) Documents."}}},requests:{title:"Requests",description:"Status of various requests originated by you in the recent past. You can check the detailed status of the request by clicking on the \u201cdownward\u201d arrow icon.",serviceName:"Service Name",status:"Status",srnUrnEid:"SRN / URN / EID",created:"Created Date",orderPVC:"Order PVC Aadhaar Card",inProcess:"In Process",stepper:{language:"Language",name:"Name",dob:"DoB",gender:"Gender",preview:"Preview",payment:"Payment"}},requestsLarge:{serviceName:"Service Name",srnUrnEid:"SRN / URN / EID",created:"Created Date",status:"Status",resume:"Resume",delete:"Delete",aadhaarUpadate:"Aadhaar Update",hof:"HoF Based Address Update",errorMessage:"Reason For Error With Description Reason For Error With Description Reason For Error With Description",description:"Dependency on SRN 0000 1234 1234 Waiting Period for Print: 2 Hours, for more clarification Dial Helpline Number: 1947"},deletePopUp:{heading:"Are you sure to delete your update request?",description:"This action will permanently delete your request from our database. Please click on 'Okay' to confirm."}},unauthenticatedDashboard:{WelcomeTo:"Welcome to ",myAadhaar:"myAadhaar",description1:"Click on ",description2:"Login ",description3:"button to explore online demographics update service, Aadhaar PVC card ordering & tracking, and more value-added services offered by UIDAI. Your mobile number is required to be registered with the Aadhaar to login.",loginCard:{loginText:"Login",desc:"Login with Aadhaar and OTP"},services:{description:"If your mobile number is not registered with Aadhaar, or you have just enrolled yourself to the world\u2019s largest identity platform, you can still use the following services.",GenericDescription:"Services which can be availed even if mobile number is not registered with Aadhaar",MobileDescription:"Services which require mobile number to be registered with Aadhaar",MoblieNotRegistered:"Mobile not Registered with Aadhaar?",StepsToRegisterText:"Please follow these steps to get it registered.",AadhaarEnrolmentUpdateCharges:"Aadhaar Enrolment & Update Charges",AadhaarEnrolmentUpdateChargesForm:"Enrolment & Update Forms",ListofDocs:"List of Supporting Documents for Aadhaar Enrolment & Update",serviceCards:{downloadAadhaar:{title:"Download Aadhaar",description:"Click here to download digitally signed and password protected electronic copy of the Aadhaar."},orderPVC:{title:"Order Aadhaar PVC Card",description:"Click here to order a secure, wallet-sized Aadhaar PVC card."},retrieveEID:{title:"Retrieve EID / Aadhaar number",description:"Click here to find out Aadhaar number or Enrolment ID (EID)."},verifyMobile:{title:"Verify Email / Mobile",description:"Click here to verify mobile and email registered with the Aadhaar."},checkAadhaarValidity:{title:"Check Aadhaar Validity",description:"Click here to validate the status of the Aadhaar."},orderPVCStatus:{title:"Check Aadhaar PVC Card Order Status",description:"Click here to check the status of the already ordered PVC card."},enrolmentAndUpdateStatus:{title:"Check Enrolment or Update Status",description:"Click here to check the status of the Enrolment or Update request."},bookAppointment:{title:"Book an Appointment",description:"Click here to book an Appointment for Enrolment or Update."},vidGenerator:{title:"VID Generator",description:"Click here to generate 16 Digit Virtual ID(VID) linked to your Aadhaar."},lec:{title:"Locate Enrolment Center",description:"Click here to search and locate nearby Aadhaar Seva Kendras."},lockUnlockAadhaar:{title:"Lock / Unlock Aadhaar",description:"Click here to temporarily lock/unlock your Aadhaar. Please use this service carefully."},authenticationHistory:{title:"Authentication History",description:"Click here to view the authentication history"},complaintStatus:{title:"Check Grievance / Feedback Status",description:"Click here to check the status of the Grievance / Feedback"},fileComplaint:{title:"Grievance and Feedback",description:"Click here to file your grievance and feedback"}}}},documentUpdate:{intentPage:{title:"Objective of Document Update Service",p1:"Dear Resident,",p2:"You are advised to strengthen your Aadhaar by updating documents in your Aadhaar database by submitting latest Proof of Identity (POI) and Proof of Address (POA) documents. The details in POI/POA documents must match with your details mentioned in your Aadhaar. This shall help you in ensuring continued accuracy of your information in the Aadhaar database.",p3:"If you have already updated the documents through any of the Aadhaar Enrolment Centers or through myAadhaar portal, please wait for its acceptance or otherwise. In case of rejection of the request submitted, you may have to update again.",p4:"If you are looking to update Address in your Aadhaar, please",p5:"click here.",p6:"A nominal charge of Rs. 25/- to be paid for the services, which is non refundable.",p7:"This service is free of cost till 14/06/2025."},howItWorks:{description:"Please read the following steps carefully. Follow the actions suggested at various steps to avoid any delay in processing or rejection of the request. If you are looking to Update your Address, Please",stepDescription:{one:"Click Here to upload your Proof of Identity (PoI) and Proof of Address (PoA) Documents.",two:"In this step, you will be asked to upload the valid POI/POA documents that contain verified details confirmed in Step 1.",three:"You have to pay \u20b9 25 (Rupees Twenty Five only) towards this service. You can make the payment through credit/debit card or net banking. This amount is non-refundable."},note:"If you are looking to update your Demographics details (Name, DoB, Gender or Address), visit nearest Aadhaar center and For Address only Update click",noteLink:"here."},currentSection:{form:{title:"Please Verify Your Demographic Details",name:"Name",gender:"Gender",dob:"Date of Birth",address:"Address",consent:"I verify that the above details are correct."},note:"If there is mismatch in any of your details, please update your Demographic details(Name, Address, DoB or Gender) at nearest nearest Aadhaar center and For Address only Update click ",noteLink:"here."},uploadSection:{confirmationPopUp:{title:"Please confirm your demographic details in the documents exactly matches with your demographic details in Aadhaar"},stepper:{verify:"Verify",upload:"Upload"},guidelines:{title:"Guidelines for uploading Documents",l1:"Document size should be less than 2 MB",l2:"Supported file Formats are: <b>JPEG, PNG</b> and <b>PDF</b>"},form:{poiTitle:"Please upload Proof Of Identity (POI) Document",poaTitle:"Please upload Proof Of Address (POA) Document"},consent:"I hereby give my consent that the information/documents provided/uploaded by me may be subjected to verification at any stage by the Government."},faq:{card:{heading:"Document Update",description_1:"Document update details",description_2:"Document update details"},guidelines:{heading_1:"Upload documents in support of identity and address",heading_2:"Free till 14/06/2025",question_1:{title:"What to submit?",content:{line_1:"Ration card, Voter identity card,  Government-issued identity card/ certificate having address, and Indian Passport serve as proof of both identity and address.",line_2:"PAN card, Driving license, Secondary or Senior School mark sheet/ School leaving certificate having photograph, Government-issued identity card/ certificate - serve as only proof of identity.",line_3:"Electricity/water/gas bill (last 3 months), Bank / Post Office passbook,  rent/ lease/ leave & license agreement serve as proof of address only.",line_4:"For detailed list of acceptable identity and address documents, please  click here.",line_5:" here"}},question_2:{title:"How to submit?",content:{line_1:"The documents can be submitted online on myAadhaar portal or by visiting any Aadhaar centre.",line_2:"For step by step procedure for submission of documents online please click here.",line_3:" here"}},main_content:{submit:"Click to submit",title:"Need Help?",videoText:"Video guide",knowMoreText:"Know More?",callText:"Call toll-free (1947)"}},one:{title:"Why should I submit the identity and address documents for my Aadhaar?",content:"Updated supporting documents for identity and address for Aadhaar enable ease of living, better service delivery and accurate authentication. Therefore, submitting recent identity and address documents is in the interest of the Aadhaar number holder."},two:{title:"What documents should I submit for my identity and address?",content:{para_1:{heading_one:"Document for both identity and address:",list_1:"(a) Ration card",list_2:"(b) Voter identity card",list_3:"(c) Kisan photo passbook",list_4:"(d) Indian passport",list_5:"(e) Government - issued identity card / certificate1, ST / SC / OBC certificate or marriage certificate, having photograph",list_6:"(f) Disability identity card / certificate of disability",list_7:"(g) Transgender identity card / certificate",list_8:"(h) Certificate issued in UIDAI standard certificate format in respect of a sex worker",list_9:"(i) Certificate issued in UIDAI standard certificate format by recognised shelter homes or orphanages",list_10:"(j) Prisoner induction document issued by Prison Officer"},para_2:{heading_one:"Document for identity:",list_1:"(a) School leaving certificate / school transfer certificate with photograph",list_2:"(b) Marksheet/certificate issued by recognised Board of Education or University with photograph",list_3:"(c) PAN/e-PAN card",list_4:"(d) Government/statutory-body/PSU-issued employee/pensioner photo identity card, pension payment order or medi-claim card",list_5:"(e) Driving licence",list_6:"(f) Freedom fighter photo identity card"},para_3:{heading_one:"Document for address:",list_1:"(a) Electricity, water, gas or telephone/mobile/broadband bill (not more than three months old)",list_2:"(b) Duly signed and stamped Scheduled Commercial Bank / Post Office passbook with photograph",list_3:"(c) Duly signed and stamped Scheduled Commercial Bank / Post Office account/credit-card statement (not more than three months old)",list_4:"(d) Valid rent, lease or leave & licence agreement",list_5:"(e) Certificate issued in UIDAI Standard Certificate format by MP, MLA, MLC, Municipal Councillor, Group 'A' or \u2018B\u2019 Gazetted Officer, EPFO Officer or Tahsildar",list_6:"(f) Certificate issued in UIDAI Standard Certificate format by Village Panchayat Head/Secretary, Village Revenue Officer or equivalent (for rural areas)",list_7:"(g) Certificate issued to a student in UIDAI Standard Certificate format by the head of the recognised educational institution concerned",list_8:"(h) Property tax receipt (not more than one year old)",list_9:"(i) Valid registered sale agreement or gift deed",list_10:"(j) Government/statutory-body/PSU-issued accommodation allotment letter (not more than one year old)",list_11:"(k) Life or medical insurance policy (not more than one year old)"}}},three:{title:"How can I submit the documents?",content:"The documents can be submitted online through  MyAadhaar Portal or at any Aadhaar Enrolment Centre. For a tutorial video in this regard, please click here https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1jne0KzFcF8 "},four:{title:"How can I submit the documents online?",content:{list_1:"Please log in to MyAadhaar Portal using your Aadhaar number and one-time password (OTP) received on your registered mobile number.",list_2:"List of supporting documents is available at https://uidai.gov.in/images/commdoc/List_of_Supporting_Document_for_Aadhaar_Enrolment_and_Update.pdf"}},five:{title:"If the address displayed in my profile does not match with my current address, what should I do?",content:"You can update your address online through myAadhaar portal or by visiting any Aadhaar Enrolment Centre by enrolling with valid POA document."},six:{title:"If any identity detail (name, gender or date of birth) does not match my actual identity details, what should I do?",content:"Please visit an Aadhaar centre with original identity documents as listed https://uidai.gov.in/images/commdoc/List_of_Supporting_Document_for_Aadhaar_Enrolment_and_Update.pdf"},seven:{title:"If I want to submit documents offline, how can I locate an Aadhaar centre?",content:{list_1:"(1) Please go to https://bhuvan.nrsc.gov.in/aadhaar/",list_2:"(2) For locating nearby Aadhaar centres, click on the \u2018Centres Nearby\u2019 tab. Enter your location details to view nearby Aadhaar centres.",list_3:"(3) For locating the Aadhaar centres within your PIN code area, click on the \u2018Search by PIN Code\u2019 tab. Enter your area PIN code to view Aadhaar centres in that area."}},eight:{title:"What is the charge for submitting the documents?",content:"For submission of documents at an Aadhaar centre, the applicable charge is Rs. 50. Submission of documents may also be done through myAadhaar portal."},nine:{title:"By when should I submit the documents? ",content:"Aadhaar number holders are suggested to update documents in Aadhaar at least once in 10 years. Once you receive any communication in this regard, it is suggested to update the documents at an early date."},ten:{title:"I am a non-resident Indian (NRI). How can I submit the documents? ",content:"You can submit the documents whenever you are in India, through online or by visiting Aadhaar Centre."}}},ssup:{howItWorks:{title:"How it Works?",description:"Please read the following steps to understand the online update process. Follow the actions suggested at various steps to avoid any delay in processing or rejection of the request.",proceedToUpdateAadhaar:"Proceed to Update Aadhaar",stepDescription:{one:"Select the Address field to update from the list. Through this online portal, you can update Address. For Name, Gender, DOB, mobile number, email and biometrics data, please visit the nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra.",two:"Please enter the required demographic data. Some of the demographic data require selection from the dropdown list. Please be careful while entering the demographics data or selecting from the dropdown options.",three:"Address update requires scanned copy of the original supporting document. Please make sure that the supporting document is in your name and valid. If you are providing a certificate in UIDAI standard format, please check for common mistakes like Issue date, Crossed sign, Stamp across Photo and No Overwriting to avoid rejection of the request.",four:"You have to pay \u20b9 50 (Rupees fifty only) towards the online update fee. You can make the payment through credit/debit card or net banking. This amount is non-refundable. In case of payment failure, you can retry the payment.",five:"You will obtain a Service Request Number (SRN) as a reference. Preserve this number to track the update request or for any future communication with UIDAI helpdesk.",six:"Your request will be verified by our internal quality check operators. At this stage provided demographics data will be checked against the supporting document. If there is a mismatch, your request is likely to be rejected.",seven:"On completion of the quality check process, you will receive an SMS notification containing the Enrolment ID an outcome.",eight:"After a few more validations by our backend software, your request processing will be completed. You will get an SMS notification on the outcome.",nine:"Normally update request is completed within 30 days with 90% service standards. However, we are improving our systems and in most likelihood, your request would be updated earlier to the mentioned time. You can check the status of the request processing by visiting myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in."}},updateSelectPage:{title:"Online Update Services",selectFields:{smallDescription:"Select Aadhaar data field(s) to update.",longDescription:"Select any of the following Aadhaar data field(s) to update.",updatesLeft:" Updates Left",noLimit:"No Limit",demoGraphics:{language:"Language",name:"Name",dob:"Date of Birth",gender:"Gender",address:"Address",hof:"HoF Based Address",document:"Document Update"}},documentDescriptionLinkText:"View Required Valid Documents related to PoI / PoA / PoB for Uploading.",proceedToUpdateAadhaar:"Proceed to Update Aadhaar",faq:"Frequently Asked Questions"},dashboard:"Dashboard",hof:{title:"Head Of Family (HOF) based Address Update",description:"Click here to proceed with Head of Family based address update.",howItWorks:{step1:"Please enter the Aadhaar number of your Head of Family to fetch the Address from Aadhaar Database. Only Residents who have attained the age of 18 or older can be considered as a HoF.",step2:"Please upload the Proof of Relationship (PoR) document that has your Name along with your Head of Family's Name clearly mentioned. Please select HoF's relationship with you, For example if HoF is your husband, select \"Husband\".",step3:"You have to pay \u20b9 50 (Rupees fifty only) towards the online update fee. You can make the payment through credit/debit card or net banking. This amount is non-refundable.",step4:"When your Head of Family logs onto their myAadhaar portal, they will receive a request for address sharing, which they can accept or deny. This option to accept / decline the request by HoF shall be valid for 30 days from the date of creation of the request."},currentSection:{title:"Details of HoF Required for update"},updateSection:{forms:{hofUid:{label:"Enter Aadhaar Number of HoF"},mobileField:{label:"Mobile Number of HoF"},documentUpload:{label:"Select Valid Supporting Document Type"},relationshipDropdown:{label:"Select HoF's Relation with the Applicant",values:{father:"Father",mother:"Mother",husband:"Husband",wife:"Wife",guardian:"Guardian",Others:"Others"}}}}},documentInfoPopup:{title:" Please upload a valid document to process your request.",identityDocumentInfo:"If the document is for Identity proof, it should be in your name and should have a photograph. Please verify that 'Name' mentioned above in the screen matches 'Name' in document you are uploading.",addressDocumentInfo:"If the document is for address proof, it should be in your name. Documents in the name of spouse, guardian, or parents will not be accepted. Please verify that 'Address' mentioned above in the screen matches 'Address' in document you are uploading.",close:"Close",continueToUpload:"Continue to Upload"},forms:{reUseDocText:"You may reuse the following already uploaded documents.",stepper:{language:"Language",Name:"Name",dob:"DOB",gender:"Gender",address:"Address",preview:"Preview",payment:"Payment"},formButtons:{back:"Back",next:"Next",makePayment:"Make Payment",retry:"Retry Payment",goToDashboard:"Go to Dashboard"},languageForm:{currentSection:{title:"Current Local Language Details",fields:{currentLocalLanguage:"Current Local Language"}},updateSection:{title:"Select New Local Language",fields:{}}},nameForm:{currentSection:{title:"Current Details",fields:{currentName:"Current Name",currentLocalName:"Current Name"}},updateSection:{title:"Details to be Updated",fields:{newName:"New Name",documentType:"Select Valid Supporting Document Type",documentTypeError:"Document type not selected",uploadDocumentLabel:"View Details & Upload Document",clear:"Clear",same_data_error:"Updated name and existing name in Aadhaar is same! Please recheck and enter correct name."}}},dobForm:{currentSection:{title:"Current Details",fields:{currentDOB:"Current Date of Birth"}},updateSection:{title:"Details to be Updated",fields:{newDOB:"New Date Of Birth to be Updated",documentType:"Select Valid Supporting Document Type",documentTypeError:"Document type not selected",uploadDocumentLabel:"View Details & Upload Document",clear:"Clear"}},confirmationPopUp:{heading:"Are you sure you want to change your date of birth to {{- dob}}?",description:"Please click on 'Okay' to confirm."}},genderForm:{currentSection:{title:"Current Details",fields:{currentGender:"Current Gender"}},updateSection:{title:"Details to be Updated",fields:{newGender:"New Gender to be Updated",genderError:"Gender not Selected"}},options:{male:"Male",female:"Female",transgender:"Transgender"},confirmationPopUp:{heading:"Are you sure you want to change your gender to {{gender}}?",description:"Please click on 'Okay' to confirm."}},addressForm:{currentSection:{title:"Current Details",fields:{currentAddress:"Current Address",currentLocalAddress:"Current Address"}},updateSection:{title:"Details to be Updated",fields:{careOf:"Care of",house:"House/Building/Apartment",street:"Street/Road/Lane",area:"Area/Locality/Sector",landmark:"Landmark",pincode:"Pincode",village:{title:"Village/Town/City",errorMsg:"Error in fetching village/town/city",nullErrorMsg:"Please select village/town/city"},postOffice:{title:"Post Office",errorMsg:"Error in fetching post office",nullErrorMsg:"Please select post office"},district:{title:"District",errorMsg:"Error in fetching district",nullErrorMsg:"Please select district"},state:{title:"State",errorMsg:"Error in fetching state",nullErrorMsg:"Please select state"},documentType:"Select Valid Supporting Document Type",documentTypeError:"Document type not selected",uploadDocumentLabel:"View Details & Upload Document",clear:"Clear"}}},preview:{fields:{newLanguage:"New Local Language",newName:"New Name",newDOB:"New Date Of Birth",newGender:"New Gender",newAddress:"New Address",newLocalName:"New Name",newLocalGender:"New Gender",newLocalAddress:"New Address",updateLanguage:"Edit Updated Local Language",updateName:"Edit Updated Name",updateDOB:"Edit Updated Date Of Birth",updateGender:"Edit Updated Gender",updateAddress:"Edit Updated Address"},edit:"Edit",supportingDocuments:"Supporting Documents",dataFields:"Updated Data Fields",transliterationText:"Allow UIDAI to correct any transliteration related inaccuracy which may have occurred.",acceptTermsText:"I hereby confirm that I have read the instructions carefully and the information provided by me to the UIDAI is true and correct .",acceptTermsText_p1:"I hereby confirm and declare that all the information and documents submitted is correct to the best of my knowledge and belief.",acceptTermsText_p2:"I understand that if the above declaration is found to be incorrect, my Aadhaar number may be deactivated and, in addition, action may be taken against me as per law.",acceptTermsText_p3:"I understand that the above information may be used, disclosed or shared in accordance with the Aadhaar (Targeted Delivery of Financial and Other Subsidies, Benefits and Services) Act, 2016 and regulations made thereunder.",acceptTermsText_p4:"I hereby give my consent for electronically obtaining information evidencing proof of identity, address, birth and/or relationship from the databases of the authorities dealing with the preparation or maintenance of such information and for sharing the above information and documents with government agencies and/or any such authority, for the purpose of verification.",acceptTermsText_p5:"I hereby agree with the Declaration.",errorPop:{error:"Error!",close:"Close"}}},payment:{paymentOptions:{text:"Please select a payment option"},makePayment:{welcomeText:"Dear Resident,",documentPaymentInfo:"You will be charged Rs. {{paymentAmount}} to process the Document Update request.",paymentInfo:"You will be charged Rs. {{paymentAmount}} to process the online update request.",linkText:"You can find more information on the Payments / Cancellation / Refunds Process here.",acceptTerms:"I hereby confirm that I have read and understood the Payments / Cancellation / Refunds Process.",poweredBy:"Powered By",popUp:{title:"Payment Policy",payment:{title:"Payment for Online Update Request",p1:"\u25cf We charge Rs 50.00 for our online update service. Rs 50 is charged irrespective of the number of demographic fields selected for update.",p2:"\u25cf For payment, we will redirect you to our payment gateway i.e. PayUBiz portal. You can use net-banking, Debit/Credit Card, UPI, or other available online instruments to make the payment."},cancel:{title:"Cancellation of Online Update Request",p1:"\u25cf A resident can cancel his update request until it is reviewed by our backend operators. On successful cancellation of request, we refund the total amount i.e Rs 50.00."},refund:{title:"Refund Policy",p1:" \u25cf We refund the total amount i.e. Rs 50.00 for successfully canceled update requests.",p2:"\u25cf In case you encounter an error while attempting payment at our payment gateway, we reconcile your transaction details with the payment gateway. If we find that money has been deducted from your bank account/credit/debit card, we initiate the refund for the total amount.",p3:"\u25cf Our refund process may take any time between a few hours to 21days."}}},paymentStatus:{transactionStatus:"Transaction Status",reason:"Reason",dateAndTime:"Payment Date & Time",amount:"Amount",failed:"Failed",success:"Success",downloadAckText:"Download Acknowledgement"},paymentPopup:{estTime:"Estimated Time",description:"Please wait while we complete the transaction and generate the acknowledge slip."}}},myHofRequests:{title:"My Head of Family(HoF) Requests",description:"Click here to check HoF based Address Sharing Requests",forms:{title:"Please type SRN and Fetch Request to respond",label:"Enter SRN",buttons:{decline:"Decline",accept:"Accept"},displayMsg:{case1:"You Have Received A Request on Above SRN from {{resident}} for Address Sharing.",case2:"You Have Approved to share your Address with {{resident}}.",case3:"You Have Declined to share your Address with {{resident}}.",case4:"No Request Found on Above SRN."},acceptScreen:{acceptMsg:"You have Accepted the request as a Head of Family for sharing your address.",declineMsg:"You have Rejected the request as a Head of Family for sharing your address."},confirmationPopUp:{rejectPrompt:"Are you sure You would like to Reject the Request As A HoF For Sharing Address?",acceptPrompt:"Are you sure You would like to Accept the Request As A HoF For Sharing Address?"}}},pvc:{oauth:{preview:{sectionHeading:"Please preview your demographic details before placing order for Aadhaar PVC card",sectionText:"In case you find any inaccuracy/missing/old/outdated information with your Aadhaar, you may opt to update your Aadhaar first by visiting the nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra or accessing the Update Aadhaar Data option from this portal",name:"Name",dob:"Date Of Birth",gender:"Gender",address:"Address"}},makePayment:{popUp:{title:"PAYMENT / CANCELLATION / REFUND POLICY",payment:{title:"Payment for Online Update and PVC Card Request",documentTitle:"Payment for Document Update",p1:"\u25cf We charge <b>\u20b9 50.00</b> for our online update service. <b>\u20b9 50.00</b> is charged irrespective of the number of demographic fields selected for update.",p2:"\u25cf UIDAI charges <b>\u20b9 50.00</b> (including taxes) for Aadhaar PVC card. The charge includes the cost of the card and delivery through Speed Post service of India Post at the registered address of the resident in Aadhaar database",p3:"\u25cf For making payment, you will be redirected to UIDAI payment gateway. You can use Netbanking, Debit/Credit Card, UPI, or other available online options to make the payment.",p4:"\u25cf A nominal charge of <b>\u20b9 25.00</b> to be paid for the services, which is <b>non-refundable</b>."},cancel:{title1:"Cancellation of Online Update Request",p1:"\u25cf A resident can only cancel her/his update request <b>until it is reviewed by our backend operators</b>. On successful cancellation of request, we would refund the total amount i.e <b>\u20b9 50.00</b>."},refund:{title:"Refund Policy",p1:"\u25cf We would refund the total amount i.e. <b>\u20b9 50.00</b> only for canceled \u201conline update requests\u201d.",p2:"\u25cf UIDAI would refund the total amount i.e. <b>\u20b9 50.00</b> in case your request for Aadhaar PVC card is not processed due to any technical reasons.",p3:"\u25cf In case you encounter any error during payment, our backend process would reconcile your transaction with the payment gateway to find out the status.",p4:"\u25cf If money has been deducted from your bank account/credit/debit card but does not reflect on the order confirmation page, our reconciliation process would verify the same and provide the correct status of the payment.",p5:"\u25cf If you have not attempted the \u201cPayment Retry\u201d option, we will reconcile the transaction for \u201cSuccessful\u201d status, then we will process your request.",p6:"\u25cf If you have attempted the \u201cPayment Retry\u201d option and completed the payment successfully, your previous transaction(s) would be reconciled. For successful duplicate transactions, a refund would be initiated.",p7:"\u25cf Our refund process may take any time between 24 hours to 10 working days."}}},generic:{form:{selectLabel:"Select 12 Digit Aadhaar Number/ 28 digit Enrolment ID",radioLabels:{uid:"Aadhaar Number",eid:"Enrolment ID Number"},textFields:{uid:"Enter Aadhaar Number",eid:"Enter 14 digit Enrolment Number",generic:"Enter Enrolment ID, SRN or URN",mobile:"Enter Mobile Number",otp:"Enter OTP",securityCode:"Enter Captcha"},checkBox:{mobile:"My mobile number is not registered",tnc:"Terms and conditions"},button:{otp:"Send OTP",submit:"Submit"},modal:{mobile:"If your Aadhaar is registered with mobile number, we would encourage you to login to myAadhaar (myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in) and place the order for PVC card.",tnc:{heading:"Please find below the approved 'Terms & Conditions' to be updated in OAC portal: ",t1:"I hereby give my consent for printing of my Aadhaar PVC card.",t2:"I understand that my printed Aadhaar PVC card will be delivered at my address, registered with Aadhaar which is complete and correct with Pincode.",t3:"I hereby agree to pay Rs 50/- (Incl GST) for Order Aadhaar PVC card service.",t4:"I understand that Aadhaar PVC card will be delivered by SPEED POST service of India Post in line with their delivery norms. Delivery status may be tracked using India Post Status Tracking services."}},note:{title:"Note:",content:{p1:"\u25cf Order Aadhaar PVC Card by paying Rs 50/-(inclusive of GST & Speed post charges).",p2:"\u25cf Use your Aadhaar Number/EID to order Aadhaar card."}}},payment:{welcomeText:"Dear Resident,",srnInfo:"Your request has been registered with SRN #",trackInfo:"Please use this number for order tracking and correspondence with UIDAI.",paymentText:"You would be charged Rs 50/-(inclusive of GST & Speed post charges) for the PVC Aadhaar card.",redirectInfo:"On clicking Make Payment button, you will be redirected to PayU Payment Gateway for online payment. On successful payment, you would be redirected back to this page for download of the Acknowledgement Slip. In case the payment fails, you can retry the payment multiple times.",button:{cancel:"Cancel",makePayment:"Make Payment"}}},status:{description:"Use this page to check the status of the new SRNs, starting with 'S' and issued by myaadhaar portal. Status of SRNs starting with number and originated with older portal are to be checked at https://resident.uidai.gov.in/check-reprint-status",srnField:"Enter SRN",table:{srn:"SRN",orderDate:"Order Date",currentStatus:"Current Status",awb:"Air Way Bill Number",dispatchDate:"Date of Dispatch",awb_subText:"You can track your order at 'www.indiapost.gov.in' using above number",demographic:"Due to privacy reasons, demographics data for the Aadhaar number can not be disclosed at the state. However, the ordered PVC card will have the latest demographics data of the Aadhaar."}}},aadharStatus:{title:"Check Enrolment or Update Status",description:{one:"Check if your Aadhaar is generated or updated.",twoEID:"The 14 digit enrolment number, printed on acknowledgement slip while physically visiting Enrolment / Update center. Sample: 1234/12345/12345",twoSRN:"\u2018S\u2019 followed by 13 digits, printed on acknowledgement slip while submitting online update request. Sample: S1234567891234",twoURN:"The 8 digit URN, printed on acknowledgement slip while submitting update request through \u2018mAadhaar\u2019 application. Sample: 12345678",twoSID:"\u2018S\u2019 followed by 27 digits, printed on acknowledgement slip while physically visiting Enrolment / Update center. Sample: S123456789123456789123456789",three:'In case if you lost EID you can retrieve lost or forgotten EID by your registered mobile number or email ID. <a href="/retrieve-eid-uid" class="click_here">Click here</a> to Retrieve EID'},optionalMessage:"Mention date and time as per the acknowledgement slip (<b>optional</b>)",withoutoptionalMessage:"Mention date and time as per the acknowledgement slip",holdMessage:"We're experiencing a delay in processing your request. As and when the issue is resolved and the request is processed, we will communicate the progress. Inconvenience caused is deeply regretted."},complaintStatus:{title:"Check Grievance / Feedback Status",form:{complaintNumber:"Enter Service Request Number",QRCid:"Qrc Id",status:"Status",ComplaintNumber:"Grievance / Feedback Number",ResolutionResponse:"Resolution Response"}},fileComplaint:{title:"Grievance and Feedback",description:"Click here to file your grievance and feedback",disclaimer:"Aadhaar, as the most commonly used digital identity, is used to avail of numerous subsidies, benefits and services. In view of the same, for maintaining the accuracy of the Aadhaar database, UIDAI had initiated an exercise for update of documents and Aadhaar information. In the course of activities undertaken to keep the Aadhaar database updated, intimations are issued from time to time to Aadhaar number holders. In this connection, it is clarified that no Aadhaar number has been cancelled. In case any Aadhaar number holder has any grievance in this regard, they may submit their feedback here. Any such grievance will be duly addressed.",form:{heading:"Please enter required details",state:"Enter State",enquirer:"Grievance / Feedback For (Self/Others)",complaintType:"Enter Grievance / Feedback Type",categoryType:"Enter Category Type",uploadDocumentLabel:"View Details & Upload Document (if any)",statusField:"Enter EID / URN",placeholder:"Dear Resident, you are requested to provide {{fields}}, to resolve your concern effectively.",error:{complaintType:"Grievance / Feedback type not selected",categoryType:"Category not selected",state:"State not selected",enquirer:"Enquirer Type not selected"}},Complaintnote:"It is strongly advised to select the right Grievance / Feedback Type for quick resolution of your grievance. Selection of wrong Grievance / Feedback Type may lead to delay in Processing or Cancellation of your request",Categorynote:"It is strongly advised to select the right Category Type for quick resolution of your grievance. Selection of wrong Category type may lead to delay in Processing or Cancellation of your request",feedbackTextArea:" Please share your feedback",feedback:"Please share your experience while filing your Grievance / Feedback by rating below"},page404:{error:"ERROR",pageNotFound:"PAGE NOT FOUND",btnText:"Visit UIDAI website for Aadhaar related information"},errorMessages:{slipApiFailed:"We're unable to proceed due to an error in generating acknowledgement slip. Please retry after sometime.",exisitingDraft:"You already have an active draft from the previous interaction with the portal. You may edit the draft request or cancel it and start afresh.",fetchingRequests:"Please wait while we fetch your previous requests from the database.",fetchApiFailed:"Couldn't fetch user request data. Something went wrong.",fetchApiFailed1:"Something went wrong while fetching requests.",fetchApiFailed2:"No Record Found.",documentPOAApiFailed:"Couldn't get list of POA documents. Something went wrong.",documentPOBApiFailed:"Couldn't get list of POB documents. Something went wrong.",documentPOIApiFailed:"Couldn't get list of POI documents. Something went wrong.",oauthFailure:"Something went wrong.",oauthFailure1:"Invalid Token.",technicalError1:"We couldn't complete your request due to temporary errors in accessing our backend services. You will be redirected to the main dashboard to resume the process.",technicalError2:"We couldn't complete your request due to temporary errors in accessing our backend services.",sessionExpired:"Session Expired! You'll be redirected to login page. Please login again.",requestDeleted:"Request cancelled successfully!"},popUpActions:{okay:"Okay",cancel:"Cancel",later:"Later",raiseGrievance:"Raise Grievance",copyCode:"Copy code",ok:"OK",close:"Close"},eaadhaarDownload:{title:"eAadhaar Download",stepper:{preview:"Preview",download:"Download"},sectionTite:"Review your Demographics Data",description:'If you wish to correct or update any of the demographics data, please visit "Update Aadhaar Online" section or nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra.',fields:{eName:"Name",eAddress:"Address",name:"Name",address:"Address",dob:"Date of Birth",gender:"Gender"},btns:{download:"Download",goToDashboard:"Go to Dashboard",retry:"Retry Download"},successPage:{congratulation:"Congratulations !!!",successText:"Your Aadhaar Card has been Successfully Downloaded",descriptionTextOne:"The Aadhaar letter PDF Password will be in 8 characters",descriptionTextTwo:"Combination of the first four letter of your name (as in Aadhaar) in CAPITAL letters and Year of Birth in YYYY format.",exampleTextOne:"Example : Your name is ANISH Y KUMAR Your Year of Birth is 1989",exampleTextTwo:"Then your e-Aadhaar password is ANIS1989"}},unauthEaadhaarDownload:{title:"eAadhaar Download",selectLabel:"Select 12 digit Aadhaar Number /16 digit Virtual ID (VID) Number / 28 digit Enrollment ID (EID) Number",radioLabels:{uid:"Aadhaar Number",eid:"Enrolment ID Number",vid:"Virtual ID Number"},textFields:{uid:"Enter Aadhaar Number",eid:"Enter 14 digit Enrolment Number",vid:"Enter Virtual ID Number",otp:"Enter OTP",securityCode:"Enter Captcha",date:"Select date",time:"Select time",srnInfo:"Enter 'S' followed by 13 digit number",urnInfo:"Enter 8 digit URN Number",sidInfo:"Enter 'S' followed by 27 digit number"},checkBox:{mask:"Do you want a masked Aadhaar?"},button:{otp:"Send OTP",submit:"Verify & Download"},messages:{otp:"OTP generated successfully!",otp2:"OTP successfully dispatched to your Aadhaar registered mobile number"}},vidGeneration:{title:"Generate or Retrieve VID",btnText:"Verify and Proceed",btnText2:"Next",response:{successText:{part1:"Your Virtual ID(VID) ",part2:"has been sent your Aadhaar registered mobile number"},subText:"In case you have changed your mobile number or wish to change your registered Email you are required to get it updated in your Aadhaar as soon as possible."},radio:{title:"Please Select",gvid:"Generate VID",rvid:"Retrieve VID"}},retrieveEID:{generic:{form:{separator:"OR",textFields:{name:"Enter Name",email:"Enter Email Address"}},status:{eid:{mobileNumber:"Your Enrollment ID(EID) {{eid}} is sent to your registered mobile number.",email:"Your Enrollment ID(EID) {{eid}} is sent to your registered email address."},uid:{mobileNumber:"Your Aadhaar number {{uid}} is sent to your registered mobile number.",email:"Your Aadhaar number {{uid}} is sent to your registered email address."}}}},checkAadhaarValidity:{title:"Check Aadhaar Validity",btnText:"Proceed",responsePage:{dataFields:{ageBand:"Age Band",gender:"Gender",state:"State",mobile:"Mobile",years:"years"},status:{exists:"Exists",notExists:"doesn't Exists",suspended:{main:"Suspended",part1:"Aadhaar number",part2:"has been deactivated under regulation 28 of the Aadhaar (Enrolment & Update) Regulations, 2016"},cancelled:{main:"Cancelled",part1:"Aadhaar number",part2:"has been cancelled under regulation 27 of the Aadhaar (Enrolment & Update) Regulations, 2016"}},aadhaar:"Aadhaar Number",descText:"Aadhaar Verification Completed"}},offlineEkyc:{title:"Offline eKYC",title1:"Create a Share Code of 4 Digits",title2:"Congratulations!!",stepper:{setCode:"Set Code",download:"Download"},button:{back:"Back",download:"Download",goToDashboard:"Go to Dashboard"},invalidShareCode:"Invalid Share Code! Please retry with correct share code.",shareCode:{title:"Create a Share Code",descText:"A ZIP file containing your eKYC will be password protected using the above Share Code. Upon clicking Download, the file will be downloaded into your device / desktop.",placeholderText:"4 - Digits Share Code to be Created"},success:{desc:"To avail the service please share the",p1:"ZIP file",p2:"Share Code",p3:"Registered Mobile Number with the service provider",summary:"This will provide Offline Aadhaar Verification facility to service providers / Offline Verification Seeking Entity (OVSE) without the need to collect or store Aadhaar number."},descTextStep1:"Aadhaar Paperless Offline e-KYC is a secure and shareable document which can be used by any Aadhaar holder for offline verification of identification. The details will contain Name, Address, Photo, Gender, DoB, hash of registered Mobile Number, hash of registered Email Address and reference id which contains last 4 digits of Aadhaar Number followed by time stamp in a digitally signed XML.",descTextStep2:"Your ZIP file for Offline eKYC has been Successfully Downloaded"},lockUnlockBiometrics:{serviceCard:{errorMessage:"Please wait while we fetch current lock/unlock status."},howItWorks:{title:"How Lock/Unlock Biometrics Works",description:"Bio Lock/Unlock feature prevents possible misuse of the Resident\u2019s Biometrics Data. Locked Biometrics prevents the use of Biometrics information for authentications. Users of this Service are cautioned to do so with care to prevent denial of Authentication services.",infoData:{stepOneDescription:" Please use this service from the Dashboard to lock your biometrics. When you lock  your biometrics (fingerprint, iris, and face)  they can no longer be used for authentication. However, OTP-based authentication would continue to be available as needed.",stepTwoDescription:" Please return to this page and proceed to Unlock Biometrics. Upon Unlocking Your Biometrics ( Fingerprint + Iris + Face ) will be enabled along with OTP based Authentication."}},selectionScreen:{unlockCard:{heading:"Please Select To Unlock",consentText:"I Understand that after unlocking my biometric, I will be able to perform biometric authentication.",label:"Unlock Biometrics"},lockCard:{heading:"Please Select To Lock",consentText:"I Understand that after locking my biometric, I will not be able to perform biometric authentication until I unlock my Biometrics.",label:"Lock Biometrics"},selectOptionError:"Kindly select only one option.",selectButton:{tempUnlock:"Unlock Biometrics Temporarily",tempUnlockInfo:"For Short Time Duration",unlock:"Unlock Biometrics Permanently",unlockInfo:"Until Next Time You Lock"}},successScreen:{tempUnlockMessage:"If you want to permanently unlock, please revisit this service from dashboard."}},lockUnlockAadhaar:{howItWorks:{title:"How Lock/Unlock Aadhaar Works",infoData:{stepOneLabel:"Step 1 of 3: ",stepOneDescription:"Before proceeding to Lock / Unlock Aadhaar, please generate a 16-digit Virtual ID (VID), as only VID has the ability to Lock / Unlock Aadhaar. You can generate your VID using the Generate Virtual ID service from the Dashboard or by sending an SMS to 1947. RVID [last 4 or 8 digits of UID] {ex: RVID 1234}. ",stepOneLinkText:"Click Here to Generate VID",stepTwoLabel:"Step 2 of 3: ",stepTwoDescription:"Once your VID has been generated, please return to this page and proceed to lock your Aadhaar with your VID, then authenticate with your VID whenever necessary, as using your Aadhaar number for authentication will be disabled once locked.",stepThreeLabel:"Step 3 of 3: ",stepThreeDescription:"Please return to this page and proceed to Unlock Aadhaar; only VID has the ability to Unlock Aadhaar, while Unlocking Aadhaar also permits Aadhaar Number-based authentication."}},formScreen:{title:"Please enter required details to Lock/Unlock Aadhaar",radioLabels:{lockAadhaar:"Lock Aadhaar",unlockAadhaar:"Unlock Aadhaar"},consent:{lockConsent:"I Understand that after locking my Aadhaar, I will be able to perform authentication using only Virtual ID (VID) and not Aadhaar Number.",unlockConsent:"I Understand that after unlocking my Aadhaar, I will be able to perform authentication using both Virtual ID (VID) and Aadhaar Number."},textFields:{name:"Enter Full Name",pincode:"Enter Pincode"}}},verifyEmailMobile:{desc:"Please Enter Required Details to Verify Email / Mobile Number",verifyMobile:"Verify Mobile Number",verifyEmail:"Verify Email Address",verifyEmailMobile:"Verify Email / Mobile"},aadharUpdateHistory:{title1:"Check your Aadhaar Update History",label1:"Record",label2:"Date of Enrolment/Update",label3:"URN/EID ",label4:"Type",list1:"Name",list2:"Mobile",list3:"Email",list4:"DOB",list5:"Gender",list6:"Address"},bankLinkingStatus:{sectionTitle:"Check Aadhaar Bank Linking Status",aadhaarNumber:"Aadhaar Number",bankLinkingStatus:"Bank Linking Status",active:"Active",inactive:"Inactive",prevBankDetails:"Previous Bank Linking Details",lastUpdatedDate:"Last Updated Date",failureMessage:"No Bank mapping record found for this Aadhaar number",successMessage:"Your Aadhaar-Bank Mapping has been done",disclaimer:"Aadhaar Linking status is fetched from NPCI Server. Under any circumstance, UIDAI shall not be responsible or liable for the correctness of the displayed status. Further, UIDAI is not storing any information fetched from NPCI server.",noRecordsAvailable:"No Records Available",checkWithBank:"Please check with your Bank to get your Aadhaar Number linked to your Bank Account"},bankSeedingStatus:{AadhaarNumber:"Aadhaar Number",BankName:"Bank Name",BankSeedingStatus:"Bank Seeding Status",LastUpdatedDate:"Last Updated Date",noRecordAlert:"Please check with your Bank to get your Aadhaar Number linked to your Bank Account",note:"The information provided through the link is fetched from the server of National Payment Corporation of India (NPCI). UIDAI is not responsible for its correctness. The information fetched is not stored by UIDAI.",ActiveText:"Active",InactiveText:"Inactive"},FAQ:{checkAadhaarPvcCardOrderStatus:[{question:"What are the different forms of Aadhaar and what are their features?",answer:"The different forms of Aadhaar are Aadhaar Letter, Aadhaar PVC card, eAadhaar and mAadhaar. All forms of Aadhaar are equally valid and acceptable."},{question:"Can I choose to have and use any form of Aadhaar?",answer:"Yes"},{question:"What is \u201cOrder Aadhaar PVC Card\u201d service?",answer:"\u201cOrder Aadhaar PVC Card\u201d is an online service launched by UIDAI which facilitates the Aadhaar holder to get their Aadhaar details printed on PVC card by paying nominal charges."},{question:"What are the security features of \u201cAadhaar PVC Card\u201d?",answer:"This card contains security features like:\n Tamper proof QR Code\n Hologram\n Micro text\n Ghost image\n Issue Date & Print Date\n Guilloche Pattern\n Embossed Aadhaar Logo"},{question:"What are the charges to be paid for \u201cAadhaar PVC Card\u201d?",answer:"Charges to be paid are Rs.50/- (Inclusive of GST & speed post charges)."},{question:"How one can raise the request for \u201cAadhaar PVC Card\u201d?",answer:"''Aadhaar PVC Card' request can be raised by visiting the UIDAI Official Website (<a href=`https://www.uidai.gov.in` target=`_blank`>https://www.uidai.gov.in</a> or https://myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in) or mAadhaar application"},{question:"How to raise request using Registered Mobile Number?",answer:" Please Visit https://uidai.gov.in or https://myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in/genricPVC.\n Enter your 12 digit Aadhaar Number (UID) or 28 digits Enrollment ID.\n Enter the security code\n Enter OTP received on registered mobile number.\n Click on the check box against \u201cTerms and Conditions\u201d. (Note: Click on hyper link to see details).\n Click on \u201cSubmit\u201d Button to complete OTP verification.\n On next screen, preview of the Aadhaar details will appear for verification by resident before placing the order for reprint.\n Click on \u201cMake payment\u201d. You will be re-directed to Payment Gateway page with payment options as Credit/Debit Card, Net banking and UPI.\n After successful payment, receipt will get generated having digital signature which can be downloaded by resident in PDF format. Resident will also get the Service Request Number via SMS.\n Aadhaar Holder can track the status of SRN till dispatch of Aadhaar Card on Check Aadhaar Card Status.\n SMS containing AWB number will also be sent once dispatched from DoP. Aadhaar Holder can further track delivery status by visiting DoP website."},{question:"How to raise request using Non-Registered/Alternate Mobile Number?",answer:"Please Visit https://uidai.gov.in or https://myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in/genricPVC Click on \u201cOrder Aadhaar Card' Service or mAadhaar application Enter your 12 digit Aadhaar Number (UID) or or 28 digits Enrollment ID. Enter the security code Click on check box \u201cIf you do not have a registered mobile number, please check in the box\u201d. Please enter Non-Registered / Alternate Mobile Number. Preview will not be available for residents ordering using non-registered mobile number. Rest of the steps for ordering remains the same."},{question:"Which modes are available to make the payment?",answer:"Presently, following online payment modes are available for making payment:-\nCredit Card\nDebit Card\nNet Banking\nUPI\nPayTM"},{question:"What is SRN?",answer:"SRN is 14 digits Service Request Number which is generated after raising request for Aadhaar update. It will be generated once you start submitting the request. Till the completion of the transaction 'resume' option shall be available."},{question:"What is AWB number?",answer:"Airway Bill Number is the tracking number that is generated by DoP i.e. India Speed Post for the assignment/product that they deliver."},{question:"What if residents want to get the Aadhaar PVC Card printed with the details that they want?",answer:"If residents want some changes in the details of printed Aadhaar letter or PVC Card, then they first have to update their Aadhaar by visiting Permanent Enrollment Center or SSUP portal (depending on update) and then raise the request because this facility can be used to get the hard copy of Aadhaar PVC Card/Letter"},{question:"How many days will it take to receive \u201cAadhaar PVC Card\u201d after creating successful request?",answer:"After receiving order for Aadhaar PVC Card from the Aadhaar number holder, UIDAI hands over printed Aadhaar Card to DoP within 5 working days (excluding the date of request). Aadhaar PVC Card is delivered via SPEED POST Service of India Post in line with existing delivery norms to the address registered in aadhaar database. An Aadhaar Number holder may track delivery status using DoP Tracking Services on <a href='https://www.indiapost.gov.in/_layouts/15/dop.portal.track' target='_blank'>https://www.indiapost.gov.in/_layouts/15/dop.portal.track</a>"}],verifyEmailMobile:[{question:"Is there any fee involved for Online updation of Demographics details?",answer:"Yes, for online update of demographic information you have to pay Rs. 50/- (including GST)."}],orderAadhaarPvcCard:[{question:"From where an Aadhaar number holder can download e-Aadhaar?",answer:"Aadhaar Number holder can download e-Aadhaar by visiting UIDAI's MyAadhaar portal- https://myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in or by using mAadhaar app for mobile phones. "}],retrieveEidAadhaarNumber:[{question:"How many times Aadhaar data can be updated?",answer:"Following limits are applicable for the update of Aadhaar information: \n\u2022 Name: Twice in Life Time \n\u2022 Gender: Once in Life Time \n\u2022 Date of Birth: Once in life time"},{question:"What changes can I do to my name in Aadhaar?",answer:"For minor corrections in your name or change in name, kindly visit nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra."},{question:"What documents are required for Online Address Update?",answer:"POA document as per supporting document list will be required. Visit <a href='https://uidai.gov.in' target='_blank'>https://uidai.gov.in.</a>"},{question:"Which are the documents required for updation in Aadhaar Address?",answer:"List of supporting documents which you can select from is available here. Please select the appropriate document from the list and provide a scan/image of the same while undertaking demographic data correction."},{question:"How can I submit my supporting documents in case of Address Update online Service?",answer:"You will be prompted to upload scan/image of the supporting document in pdf or jpeg format in the Update Address online Service. Please upload correct supporting document for processing of your request. For certain documents like Passport, Rent and Property agreement, image of multiple pages would be required."},{question:"Can I update my local language through Update Aadhaar online Service?",answer:"At present you can not update your local language through online portal."},{question:"Can I update my date of birth through Update Aadhaar online Service?",answer:"No, to update Date of Birth (DoB) kindly visit nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra with DoB proof document."},{question:"I have already updated Date of Birth in my Aadhaar once. Can I update/ correct it?",answer:"No. You can update your Date of Birth (DoB) only once. Further Date of Birth (DoB) can be changed under exceptional circumstances, kindly call 1947 in this regard."},{question:"Does submission of request guarantee update of demographic information?",answer:"Submission of information does not guarantee update of Aadhaar data. Changes submitted through Update Aadhaar online Service are subjected to verification and validation by the UIDAI and after validation only the change request is processed further for Aadhaar update."},{question:"I have lost my mobile number/ do not possess the number that I enrolled with Aadhaar. How should I submit my update request?",answer:"In case you have lost/do not possess the mobile number anymore that is registered with Aadhaar, you have to personally visit the nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra for updation of mobile number."},{question:"Will my Aadhaar number get changed after updation?",answer:"No, your Aadhaar number will remain same even after the update."},{question:"I want to cancel the update request. Will I be able to do it?",answer:"A resident can cancel the update request from the \u2018Requests\u2019 space in the myAadhaar dashboard until the request is picked up for further processing. If cancelled, the amount paid will be refunded to the account within 21 days."},{question:"Where can I see all my update requests? ",answer:"A resident can view his/her update requests inside the \u2018Requests\u2019 space inside the myAadhaar dashboard."},{question:"How do I add my father\u2019s / husband\u2019s name to my address?",answer:"Relationship details are a part of address field in Aadhaar. This has been standardized to C/o (Care of). Filling this is optional."}],eaadhaarDownload:[{question:"What is e-Aadhaar?",answer:"e-Aadhaar is a password protected electronic copy of Aadhaar, digitally signed by UIDAI."},{question:"Is e-Aadhaar equally valid like physical copy of Aadhaar?",answer:"As per Aadhaar Act, e-Aadhaar is equally valid like Physical Copy of Aadhaar for all purposes. For validity of eAadhaar, please visit UIDAI circular- <a href='https://uidai.gov.in/images/ uidai_om_on_e_aadhaar_validity.pdf' target='_blank'>https://uidai.gov.in/images/ uidai_om_on_e_aadhaar_validity.pdf</a>"},{question:"What is Masked Aadhaar?",answer:"Masked Aadhaar implies replacing of first 8 digits of Aadhaar number with \u201cxxxx-xxxx\u201d while only last 4 digits of the Aadhaar Number are visible."},{question:"How to validate digital signatures in e-Aadhaar?",answer:"Please visit Aadhaar YouTube Channel and watch tutorial link on <a href='https://youtu.be/aVNfUNIccZs?si=ByW1O6BIPMwc0seL' target='_blank'>https://youtu.be/aVNfUNIccZs?si=ByW1O6BIPMwc0seL</a>"},{question:"What Is the Password of e-Aadhaar?",answer:"Password of eAadhaar is a combination of the first 4 letters of name in CAPITAL and the year of birth (YYYY).<br/><b>For Example:</b>\nExample 1<ol><li>Name: SURESH KUMAR</li><li>Year of Birth: 1990</li><li>Password: SURE1990</li></ol>\nExample 2<ol><li>Name: SAI KUMAR</li><li>Year of Birth: 1990</li><li>Password: SAIK1990</li></ol>\nExample 3<ol><li>Name: P. KUMAR</li><li>Year of Birth: 1990</li><li>Password: P.KU1990</li></ol>\nExample 4<ol><li>Name: RIA</li><li>Year of Birth: 1990</li><li>Password: RIA1990</li></ol>"},{question:"What supporting software needed to open e-Aadhaar?",answer:"Resident needs 'Adobe Reader' to view e-Aadhaar. You have 'Adobe Reader' installed in your System. To install Adobe Reader in the System\nvisit <a href='https://get.adobe.com/reader/' target='_blank'>https://get.adobe.com/reader/</a>"},{question:"How can an Aadhaar Number holder download e-Aadhaar?",answer:"An Aadhaar Number holder can download e-Aadhaar by following three ways.\nBy Using Enrollment Number:\nBy Using Aadhaar No:\nBy using VID:\nOTP for downloading eAadhaar will be received on registered mobile number."}],bookAnAppointment:[{question:"What are the grievance redressal channels in UIDAI?",answer:"Individuals can reach UIDAI through multiple channels viz. Phone, Email, Chat, Letter/Post, Web Portal, Walk in and Social Media for their grievance redressal.\nThe detailed information about available channels are as below:\n Phone Call (Toll Free Number) -\nIndividuals can contact UIDAI Toll Free Number (1947) for concerns related to Aadhaar. UIDAI contact center consists of a self service IVRS (Interactive Voice Response system) and Individual Support Executive based assistance. Individual can choose any of below mentioned language for communication as per their ease.\n Hindi\n5. Kannada\n9. Guajarati\n English\n6. Malayalam\n10. Marathi\n Telugu\n Assamese\n Punjabi\n4. Tamil\n Bengali\n Odia\nTimings:\na) Availing of self service through IVRS: Services through IVRS can be availed in self service mode on 24X7 basis.\nb) Support Executive assistance: This service can be availed from Monday - Saturday: 7 AM to 11 PM,  Sunday: 8 AM to 5 PM.\nGeneral Queries are resolved by Contact Center Executive through UIDAI approved Standard Responses and complaints are assigned to concerned Divisions/Regional Offices of UIDAI on real time basis. These complaints are examined internally at concerned Division/Regional Offices of UIDAI for effective resolution and communication thereafter to the individual.\n2. Chatbot (Aadhaar Mitra) \u2013 Individuals can raise their concern related to Aadhaar through UIDAI chatbot service 'Aadhaar Mitra' which is available on UIDAI\u2019s Official website This chatbot is trained to respond to the queries and aimed at improving the individual experience.\n3. UIDAI Web Portal \u2013 Individuals can lodge and check the status of their grievance on UIDAI website under Grievance and Feedback & Check Grievance / Feedback Status respectively.. \n Email \u2013 Individuals can send email to help@uidai.gov.in for any queries and complaint related to Aadhaar.\n Walk-In at Regional Offices: Individuals can directly walk in to the respective regional offices according to their state for the resolution of their queries or submission of complaints related to Aadhaar.\n6. Post/Letter: Individuals can lodge their grievances in UIDAI HO or Regional offices through post or submit application by hand. The concerned Regional Office/ division will take necessary steps to resolve the grievance.\n Public Grievance Portal (CPGRAMS) of the Government of India: Grievances can be lodged at UIDAI through Centralized Public Grievance Redress and Monitoring System (CPGRAMS).This is an online platform available for the citizens 24x7.\n Social Media: Grievances may be lodged through multiple social media platforms like Twitter, Facebook, You tube, Instagram etc. Individual can upload a post related to their concern/grievance tagging the UIDAI or DM the support page on different social media streams."},{question:"Are the service charges different for Aadhaar Seva Kendras?",answer:"No, the charges for Aadhaar Services are same across all the Aadhaar centres in the country including Aadhaar Seva Kendras .\nFor charges please refer : Aadhaar Enrolment & Update Charges"},{question:"Can I reschedule/ cancel my appointment?",answer:"Yes, you can reschedule the appointment before 24 hours by logging into the appointment portal with the same mobile number/ email ID (as given earlier)."},{question:"What services I can avail from Aadhaar Seva Kendra?",answer:"Aadhaar Seva Kendras provides all type of Aadhaar services such as\n New Enrolment for all age group.\n Update of any demographic Information (Name, Address, Gender, Date of Birth, Mobile number and Email Id).\n Update of biometric information (Photo, Fingerprints and Iris Scans) .\n Mandatory Biometric Update of children (attaining the age of 5 and 15 years).\n Document update (POI and POA) .\n Find & Print Aadhaar."},{question:"What are the timings of UIDAI ASKs (Aadhaar Seva Kendras)?",answer:"Aadhaar Seva Kendras are open all 7 days of the week excluding national/regional holidays. Normally it functions from 9:30 AM to 5:30 PM (IST).\nAadhaar Enrolment Centres other than UIDAI ASKs follow timings as defined by their respective registrars. Individuals seeking enrolment/ Aadhaar number holders may contact their nearby Aadhaar Enrolment Centre for more information."},{question:"What is Aadhaar Seva Kendra (ASK)?",answer:"\u2018Aadhaar Seva Kendra\u2019 or ASK is a single-stop destination for all Aadhaar services for the residents. ASK offer dedicated Aadhaar enrolment and update services to residents in a state-of-the-art environment. The Aadhaar Seva Kendra offers a comfortable air-conditioned environment to residents. All ASK are wheelchair friendly and have special provisions to service the elderly and specially abled. More info on ASKs is available here: uidai.gov.in website."},{question:"Where can I find the list of UIDAI ASKs (Aadhaar Seva Kendras)?",answer:"A consolidated list of all functional ASKs is available at: Aadhaar Seva Kendra List\nThese ASKs are available in addition to Aadhaar Enrolment Centres already run by Banks, Post Offices, CSC, BSNL and State Governments."}],checkEnrolmentUpdateStatus:[{question:"What details can I update through Update Aadhaar online Service?",answer:"Through this online portal, you can perform only Address and Document update. For any other update, kindly visit the nearest Aadhaar Seva Kendra."}],checkAadhaarValidity:[{question:"How Aadhaar PVC Card is different from Aadhaar Letter?",answer:"Aadhaar letter is laminated paper based document issued to the Aadhaar number holders after enrolment or update. Aadhaar PVC Card is PVC based durable and easy to carry card with multiple security features. Aadhaar PVC card is equally valid."}],lockUnlockAadhaar:[{question:"My update request got rejected for invalid documents. What does this mean?",answer:"The document you use for Online Address Update should be:\n\u2022 Valid document as per <a href='https://uidai.gov.in' target='_blank'>https://uidai.gov.in</a>.\n\u2022 The document uploaded is in the name of the resident.\n\u2022 Image uploaded should be clear and colored scan of original document.\nEnsure that you follow the above before you create a new update request."},{question:"What is Aadhaar (UID) Lock & Unlock?",answer:"For a resident, security and privacy of personal data is always a primary concern. To strengthen the security of his/her Aadhaar number and to provide control to the resident, UIDAI provide a mechanism of locking and unlocking Aadhaar number (UID).\nResident can lock his or her Aadhaar (UID) via UIDAI website www.myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in or through mAadhaar app.\nBy doing this Resident cannot perform any sort of Authentication using UID, UID Token & VID for Biometrics, Demographic & OTP modality\nIf resident wants to unlock UID he/she can do so by using latest VID, through UIDAI website or mAadhaar app.\nAfter unlocking Aadhaar (UID), resident can perform authentication using UID, UID Token & VID."},{question:"How can resident Lock UID?",answer:"For Locking UID, Resident should have 16 digit VID number and it's a pre-requisite for locking. If resident don't have VID can generate via SMS Service or UIDAI website (www.myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in).\nSMS Service. GVID space last 4 or 8 digit of UID. SMS to 1947.Ex-GVID 1234.\nResident may visit UIDAI website <a href='https://resident.uidai.gov.in/aadhaar-lockunlock' target='_blank'>https://resident.uidai.gov.in/aadhaar-lockunlock</a> Under My Aadhaar tab, Click on Aadhaar Lock & Unlock services. Select UID Lock Radio Button and enter UID Number, Full Name, and Pin Code as in latest details and enter Security code. Click on Send OTP and click on submit. Your UID will be locked successfully."},{question:"How can resident Unlock UID?",answer:"For Unlocking UID resident should have latest 16 digit VID and if resident forgot 16 digit VID he can retrieve latest VID through SMS services\nRVID Space last 4 or 8 digit of UID. SMS to 1947. Ex- RVID 1234\nTo unlock UID, resident may visit UIDAI website <a href='https://resident.uidai.gov.in/aadhaar-lockunlock' target='_blank'>https://resident.uidai.gov.in/aadhaar-lockunlock</a> , select Unlock radio button, Enter Latest VID and security Code and click on send OTP and click on Submit. Your UID will be unlocked successfully.\nResident may also use Aadhaar lock or unlock service through mAadhaar app."}],grievanceAndFeedback:[],generateOrRetrieveVid:[{question:"I forgot my VID. How can I get it after locking UID?",answer:"After Locking UID if resident forgot VID, Resident can make use of SMS service to Retrieve 16 digit VID. Resident will receive VID on his/her register mobile number.\nSend SMS to 1947 from Aadhaar Register mobile number,\nRVID Space last 4 or 8 digit of UID.\nEx:- RVID 1234"},{question:"What is Virtual ID (VID)?",answer:"VID is a temporary, revocable 16-digit random number mapped with the Aadhaar number. VID can be used in lieu of Aadhaar number whenever authentication or e-KYC services are performed. Authentication may be performed using VID in a manner similar to using Aadhaar number. It is not possible to derive Aadhaar number from VID."},{question:"How does a resident obtain VID?",answer:"VID can be generated only by the Aadhaar number holder. They can also replace (generate a new VID) their VID from time to time. At any given time only one VID will be valid for an Aadhaar number. UIDAI provide various options to Aadhaar number holders to generate their VID, retrieve their VID in case they forget, and replace their VID with a new number. These options will be made available via UIDAI\u2019s website (www.myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in) , eAadhaar download, mAadhaar mobile application, etc.\nVID can also be generated by sending an SMS to the Aadhaar helpline number 1947. Resident will have to type \u201cGVIDLast 4 digits of Aadhaar Number\u201d and send it to 1947 through the registered Mobile Number."},{question:"Can anyone else generate VID for me?",answer:"No other entity like AUA/KUA can generate VID on behalf of Aadhaar number holder. The VID can be generated by Aadhaar number holder by himself/herself only. Aadhaar number holder will receive the VID through SMS on registered mobile number."},{question:"What if an Aadhaar number holder forgets VID? Can he/she obtain again?",answer:"Yes, UIDAI provide multiple ways to generate new and/or retrieve current VID. These options are made available via UIDAI\u2019s website (www.myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in) , eAadhaar, mAadhaar mobile application, SMS, etc.\nFor retrieval of VID, Aadhaar number holder may send SMS to the Aadhaar helpline number 1947. Resident will have to type \u201cRVID Last 4 digits of Aadhaar Number\u201d and send it to 1947 through the registered Mobile Number."},{question:"Can VID be used for OTP or biometrics or demographics authentication?",answer:"Yes. VID can be used in lieu of Aadhaar number to perform Aadhaar Authentication."},{question:"In case of VID, do I need to provide consent for authentication?",answer:"Yes, Aadhaar number holder consent is necessary for VID based authentication. Agency is required to inform the Aadhaar number holder the purpose for authentication and collect explicit consent for performing authentication."},{question:"Can an agency store VID?",answer:"No. Since VID is temporary and can be changed by the Aadhaar number holder, storing VID has no value. Agencies should not store VID in any database or logs."},{question:"Will re-generation of VID lead to the same VID or a different VID?",answer:"After the minimum validity period (currently set as 1 calender day or after midnight 12), Aadhaar number holder may requests regeneration of a new VID. In this way, new VID will be generated and the previous VID will be deactivated.\nIn case, if resident opts for retrieval of VID, the last active VID will be sent to the Aadhaar number holder through SMS. Resident will have to type \u201cRVIDLast 4 digits of Aadhaar Number\u201d and send it to 1947 through the registered Mobile Number."}],checkGrievanceFeedbackStatus:[{question:"What is the expiry period of VID?",answer:"At this time there is no expiry period defined for VID. VID will be valid till the time a new VID is generated by the Aadhaar number holder."}]}},Ut={dashboard:{header:{title:"\u0aae\u0abe\u0ab0\u0acb \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0",profile:{aadhaarTagLine:"\u0aae\u0ac7\u0ab0\u0abe \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0, \u0aae\u0ac7\u0ab0\u0ac0 \u0aaa\u0ab9\u0ac7\u0a9a\u0abe\u0aa8",clickToFlip:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0a95\u0abe\u0ab0\u0acd\u0aa1 \u0aab\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0aaa \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb",logOut:"\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a97 \u0a86\u0a89\u0a9f"}},services:{title:"\u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe\u0a93",description:"\u0a93\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0abe\u0a87\u0aa8 \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe\u0a93\u0aa8\u0acb \u0aa8\u0ac0\u0a9a\u0ac7\u0aa8\u0acb \u0a95\u0ab2\u0a97\u0ac0 \u0a8d\u0a95\u0acd\u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab8. \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a89\u0aaa\u0ab2\u0aac\u0acd\u0aa7 \u0a9b\u0ac7. \u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe-\u0ab5\u0abf\u0ab6\u0abf\u0ab7\u0acd\u0a9f \u0aaa\u0ac3\u0ab7\u0acd\u0aa0 \u0aaa\u0ab0 \u0aa8\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abf\u0a97\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a9f\u0ac7\u0aac \u0aaa\u0ab0 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb",serviceCards:{downloadAadhaar:{title:"\u0aa1\u0abe\u0a89\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0acb\u0aa1 \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0",description:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0ac0 \u0aa1\u0abf\u0a9c\u0abf\u0a9f\u0ab2 \u0ab8\u0ab9\u0ac0 \u0aa5\u0aaf\u0ac7\u0ab2 \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0aaa\u0abe\u0ab8\u0ab5\u0ab0\u0acd\u0aa1\u0aa5\u0ac0 \u0ab8\u0ac1\u0ab0\u0a95\u0acd\u0ab7\u0abf\u0aa4 \u0a87\u0ab2\u0ac7\u0a95\u0acd\u0a9f\u0acd\u0ab0\u0acb\u0aa8\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0acb\u0aaa\u0ac0 \u0aa1\u0abe\u0a89\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0acb\u0aa1 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},orderPVC:{title:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0aaa\u0ac0\u0ab5\u0ac0\u0ab8\u0ac0 \u0a95\u0abe\u0ab0\u0acd\u0aa1\u0aa8\u0acb \u0a93\u0ab0\u0acd\u0aa1\u0ab0 \u0a86\u0aaa\u0acb",description:"\u0ab8\u0ac1\u0ab0\u0a95\u0acd\u0ab7\u0abf\u0aa4, \u0ab5\u0ac9\u0ab2\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0a95\u0aa6\u0aa8\u0abe \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0aaa\u0ac0\u0ab5\u0ac0\u0ab8\u0ac0 \u0a95\u0abe\u0ab0\u0acd\u0aa1\u0aa8\u0acb \u0a93\u0ab0\u0acd\u0aa1\u0ab0 \u0a86\u0aaa\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},updateAadhaarOnline:{updateAadhaarOnline:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0a93\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0abe\u0a88\u0aa8 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb",updateAadhaar:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb",headerTitle:"\u0a95\u0ac3\u0aaa\u0abe \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ac0\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0a93\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0abe\u0a88\u0aa8 \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f\u0aa8\u0acb \u0aaa\u0acd\u0ab0\u0a95\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0aaa\u0ab8\u0a82\u0aa6 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb",title:"\u0ab8\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0abe\u0aae\u0ac1\u0a82 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f",description:"\u0aa4\u0aae\u0abe\u0ab0\u0abe \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0ac1\u0a82 \u0ab8\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0abe\u0aae\u0ac1\u0a82 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb. \u0a85\u0aa8\u0acd\u0aaf \u0a95\u0acb\u0a88\u0aaa\u0aa3 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7, \u0a95\u0ac3\u0aaa\u0abe \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ac0\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0aa8\u0a9c\u0ac0\u0a95\u0aa8\u0abe \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe \u0a95\u0ac7\u0aa8\u0acd\u0aa6\u0acd\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0ac0 \u0aae\u0ac1\u0ab2\u0abe\u0a95\u0abe\u0aa4 \u0ab2\u0acb"},bankLinkingStatus:{title:"\u0aac\u0ac7\u0a82\u0a95 \u0ab2\u0abf\u0a82\u0a95\u0abf\u0a82\u0a97 \u0ab8\u0acd\u0aa5\u0abf\u0aa4\u0abf",description:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0aac\u0ac7\u0a82\u0a95 \u0a96\u0abe\u0aa4\u0abe\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0a9c\u0acb\u0aa1\u0ab5\u0abe\u0aa8\u0ac0 \u0ab8\u0acd\u0aa5\u0abf\u0aa4\u0abf \u0aa4\u0aaa\u0abe\u0ab8\u0ab5\u0abe \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},generateVirtualID:{title:"\u0ab5\u0ab0\u0acd\u0a9a\u0acd\u0aaf\u0ac1\u0a85\u0ab2 \u0a86\u0a88\u0aa1\u0ac0 \u0aac\u0aa8\u0abe\u0ab5\u0acb",description:"\u0ab5\u0ab0\u0acd\u0a9a\u0acd\u0aaf\u0ac1\u0a85\u0ab2 \u0a86\u0a88\u0aa1\u0ac0 (\u0ab5\u0ac0\u0a86\u0a88\u0aa1\u0ac0) \u0aa8\u0acb \u0a89\u0aaa\u0aaf\u0acb\u0a97 \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0aa8\u0a82\u0aac\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0ac0 \u0a9c\u0a97\u0acd\u0aaf\u0abe\u0a8f \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ac0 \u0ab6\u0a95\u0abe\u0aaf \u0a9b\u0ac7. 16 \u0a85\u0a82\u0a95\u0aa8\u0abe \u0ab0\u0ac7\u0aa8\u0acd\u0aa1\u0aae \u0ab5\u0ac0\u0a86\u0a87\u0aa1\u0ac0 \u0aa1\u0abe\u0a89\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0acb\u0aa1 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},offlineEkyc:{title:"\u0a91\u0aab\u0ab2\u0abe\u0a87\u0aa8 \u0a87\u0a95\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe\u0aaf\u0ab8\u0ac0",description:"\u0a93\u0aab\u0ab2\u0abe\u0a87\u0aa8 \u0a93\u0ab3\u0a96 \u0a9a\u0a95\u0abe\u0ab8\u0aa3\u0ac0 \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a89\u0aaa\u0aaf\u0acb\u0a97\u0aae\u0abe\u0a82 \u0ab2\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe\u0aa4\u0abe \u0ab8\u0ac1\u0ab0\u0a95\u0acd\u0ab7\u0abf\u0aa4 \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0ab6\u0ac7\u0ab0 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aaf\u0acb\u0a97\u0acd\u0aaf \u0a87\u0a95\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe\u0aaf\u0ab8\u0ac0 \u0aa6\u0ab8\u0acd\u0aa4\u0abe\u0ab5\u0ac7\u0a9c\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0a8d\u0a95\u0acd\u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab8 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},lockUnlockBiometrics:{title:"\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 / \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 \u0aac\u0abe\u0aaf\u0acb\u0aae\u0ac7\u0a9f\u0acd\u0ab0\u0abf\u0a95\u0acd\u0ab8",description:"\u0aa4\u0aae\u0abe\u0ab0\u0ac0 \u0aac\u0abe\u0aaf\u0acb\u0aae\u0ac7\u0a9f\u0acd\u0ab0\u0abf\u0a95 \u0aae\u0abe\u0ab9\u0abf\u0aa4\u0ac0\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab8\u0acd\u0aa5\u0abe\u0aaf\u0ac0 \u0ab0\u0ac2\u0aaa\u0ac7 \u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 / \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},lockUnlockAadhaar:{title:"\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 / \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0",description:"\u0aa4\u0aae\u0abe\u0ab0\u0abe \u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab8\u0acd\u0aa5\u0abe\u0aaf\u0ac0 \u0ab0\u0ac2\u0aaa\u0ac7 \u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 / \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ab2\u0ac9\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb. \u0a95\u0ac3\u0aaa\u0abe \u0a95\u0ab0\u0ac0\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0a86 \u0ab8\u0ac7\u0ab5\u0abe\u0aa8\u0acb \u0a95\u0abe\u0ab3\u0a9c\u0ac0\u0aaa\u0ac2\u0ab0\u0acd\u0ab5\u0a95 \u0a89\u0aaa\u0aaf\u0acb\u0a97 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},paymentHistory:{title:"\u0a9a\u0ac1\u0a95\u0ab5\u0aa3\u0ac0 \u0a87\u0aa4\u0abf\u0ab9\u0abe\u0ab8",description:"\u0a9a\u0ac1\u0a95\u0ab5\u0aa3\u0ac0 \u0a85\u0aa8\u0ac7 \u0ab0\u0abf\u0aab\u0a82\u0aa1\u0aa8\u0ac0 \u0ab8\u0acd\u0aa5\u0abf\u0aa4\u0abf \u0a9c\u0acb\u0ab5\u0abe \u0aae\u0abe\u0a9f\u0ac7 \u0a85\u0ab9\u0ac0\u0a82 \u0a95\u0acd\u0ab2\u0abf\u0a95 \u0a95\u0ab0\u0acb"},aadharUpdateHistory:{title:"\u0a86\u0aa7\u0abe\u0ab0 \u0a85\u0aaa\u0aa1\u0ac7\u0a9f \u0a87\u0aa4\u0abf\u0ab9\u0abe\u0ab8",description:"\u0aa4\u0aae\u0abe